  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "Investors saw online books, internet broadcasting and networking equipment as signs of a changing economy. Taiwan’s election and scientific discoveries competed for attention.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The price paid and the full five-year path mattered. Spreading money across many companies reduced dependence on these three badly hit shares.",
    "what_faded_away": "The number of people downloading a story did not reveal a software or networking company’s future return. Exciting new habits were not automatic stock-market gains.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "Nobody knew the size of the losses ahead. The internet’s importance did not make every share price reasonable or every company a winner.",
